  "verdict": "void",
  "section": "20",
  "quote": "Subsection (1) applies even if the tenant was aware of a state of non-repair or a contravention of a standard before entering into the tenancy agreement.",
  "reason": "Under section 20, the landlord's statutory duty to maintain the rental unit in a good state of repair applies even if the tenant knew about the defects before signing the tenancy agreement. Because this clause attempts to relieve the landlord of that repair obligation for visible defects, it is inconsistent with the Act and therefore void under section 4(1)."
}

